-- Runtime confirmation of the same SMT-LIB FP equality claims
-- tests/solver/float32.rs proves symbolically: `=` is reflexive even for
-- NaN, `+0.0f`/`-0.0f` are distinct, and ordered comparisons are false for
-- any NaN operand (docs/design-decisions.md's `Float32` section).
main : -> Bool
main() = (nan32 == nan32) and (0.0f != -0.0f) and (not (nan32 < nan32)) and (1.0f < 2.0f)
